## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | flutter_app/lib/services/project_folder_channel.dart | 🚨 blocking the persisted mount never restores on windows linux — projectmountstore load rejects the empty bookmark the selector ops persist the pr s restore contract windows linux restore directly — nothing to re grant persisted across restarts is dead code on the platforms this pr targets the chain 1 projectfolderselectorops pickdirectory always returns an empty bookmark project folder channel dart 88 dart return path path bookmark 2 pickandapplyprojectmount persists it verbatim → project mount json gets path bookmark 3 on the next start mounteddesktopenv calls projectmountstore load baseenv whose guard rejects exactly that record project mount store dart 39 dart if bookmark is string bookmark isempty return null → stored null → a fresh wrapper is returned mountedroot null and mountunavailable null — the mount is dropped silently not even the stale mount note is surfaced reproduced against this pr head linux vm test the production round trip — pick via selector bookmark → save → simulated restart → createdesktopenv persisted record path tmp fah pr2143 host sdczhj bookmark scoped false after restart mountedroot null mountunavailable null expected tmp fah pr2143 host sdczhj actual null blast radius beyond restore setprojectmountscoped also loads through the same guard so the restrict tools to this folder toggle silently no ops for selector mounts too macos is unaffected channel bookmarks are never empty why the existing tests missed it every fake in env factory io test dart project mount test dart stores a non empty bookmark bm ym9va21hcms no test round trips the real store with the the selector ops produce fix either accept the empty bookmark in projectmountstore load — if bookmark is string return null — an empty bookmark is a legitimate selector platform value that is exactly what the projectfolderselectorops doc comment already asserts about the store or persist a non empty sentinel from projectfolderselectorops either way please add a round trip test selector bookmark → save → load so the store contract is pinned |
| F2 | open | IMPORTANT | lib/src/env/io_execution_env.dart | ⚠️ important the separator split also eats literal backslashes in posix file names — posix behavior unchanged does not hold io execution env dart 271 dart name resolved split regexp r last on posix a backslash is a legal ordinary character in a file name — it is not a separator splitting on unconditionally corrupts such names reproduced on linux against this pr head file weird name txt fileinfo name → name txt expected weird name txt every basename consumer regresses for these names — the files browser joins dir name back into a path so the entry cannot be opened renamed listdir also now sorts by the truncated tail the changelog entry posix behavior unchanged is not accurate for this input class note the new bare names test cannot catch it on posix ci real posix entries never contain so the isnot contains r assertion passes trivially fix options 1 no new dependency — split platform conditionally dart name platform iswindows resolved split regexp r last resolved split last 2 style aware basename — promote path from dev dependencies to dependencies it already resolves transitively and use p basename resolved which treats as a separator only under the windows style please also add a posix test for a backslash containing file name weird name txt → name weird name txt so the platform split stays pinned |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

diff --git a/flutter_app/lib/services/project_folder_channel.dart b/flutter_app/lib/services/project_folder_channel.dart
index 4848cde516..cd37c8b37e 100644
--- a/flutter_app/lib/services/project_folder_channel.dart
+++ b/flutter_app/lib/services/project_folder_channel.dart
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 import 'package:flutter/foundation.dart'
     show TargetPlatform, defaultTargetPlatform, kIsWeb, visibleForTesting;

+import 'package:file_selector/file_selector.dart';
 import 'package:flutter/services.dart';

 /// Native project-folder operations: directory picking plus the
@@ -69,3 +70,42 @@ final class ProjectFolderChannelOps implements ProjectFolderOps {
     await _channel.invokeMethod<void>('stopAccessing', bookmark);
   }
 }
+
+/// The desktop file-selector-backed ops (Windows/Linux): the native folder
+/// dialog through `file_selector` (file_selector_windows is a compiled
+/// plugin in the Windows runner) without security-scoped bookmarks — the
+/// bookmark is always the empty string and the access lifecycle is a
+/// success no-op, matching how [ProjectMountStore] persists the mount on
+/// platforms that have no sandbox to re-grant.
+final class ProjectFolderSelectorOps implements ProjectFolderOps {
+  /// Creates the selector-backed ops.
+  const ProjectFolderSelectorOps();
+
+  @override
+  Future<({String path, String bookmark})?> pickDirectory() async {
+    final path = await getDirectoryPath();
+    if (path == null || path.isEmpty) return null;
+    return (path: path, bookmark: '');
+  }
+
+  @override
+  Future<bool> startAccessing(String bookmark) async => true;
+
+  @override
+  Future<void> stopAccessing(String bookmark) async {}
+}
+
+/// The default [ProjectFolderOps] per platform: the security-scoped
+/// channel on macOS/iOS (sandbox bookmarks), the plain file selector on
+/// Windows/Linux, null on web/embedded targets.
+ProjectFolderOps? defaultProjectFolderOps() {
+  if (kIsWeb) return null;
+  if (defaultTargetPlatform == TargetPlatform.windows ||
+      defaultTargetPlatform == TargetPlatform.linux) {
+    return const ProjectFolderSelectorOps();
+  }
+  if (ProjectFolderChannelOps.isSupported) {
