commit 19da194d3927da0fa49a96816a740ba932b6b82e
Author: Fa Agent <fa@fa1.dev>
Date:   Fri Nov 13 20:37:28 2026 +0300

    fix(2143-review): accept empty mount bookmarks; POSIX-safe FileInfo basename

    Review findings on PR #2143:
    - ProjectMountStore.load rejected the persisted empty bookmark that
      Windows/Linux file selectors produce (no security-scoped bookmark on
      those platforms), silently killing the mount restore and the
      scoped-folder toggle. Empty strings now load; macOS keeps real
      bookmarks. Round-trip test with bookmark: '' included.
    - FileInfo.name split on both separators unconditionally, truncating
      POSIX names that legally contain backslashes (weird\name.txt ->
      name.txt). The double-separator split is now Windows-only; POSIX
      splits on '/' alone. POSIX regression test included.

